            "id": "14006060",
            "headline": "Horizon Industrial Parks raises Rs 1,168 crore from anchors ahead of Rs 2,600-crore IPO",
            "heading": "Horizon Industrial Parks raises Rs 1,168 crore from anchors ahead of Rs 2,600-crore IPO",
            "intro": "Horizon Industrial Parks IPO | The Rs 2,600-crore initial public offering is set to open for public subscription on August 17 and close on August 19.",
            "body": "Blackstone-backed Horizon Industrial Parks has raised Rs 1,167.8 crore from 54 anchor investors, including Morgan Stanley, Carmignac, Millennium Management, Societe Generale, Citigroup Global and Viridian Asset Management, ahead of its Rs 2,600-crore initial public offering (IPO).\r\n\r\nThe industrial and logistics infrastructure developer allocated 19.46 crore equity shares to anchor investors at the upper end of its IPO price band of Rs 57-60 per share on August 14.\r\n\r\nThe IPO will open for public subscription on August 17 and close on August 19. The issue comprises entirely a fresh issue of shares.\r\n\r\nHorizon Industrial Parks is owned and managed by three Blackstone affiliates, which collectively hold an 88.74 percent stake in the company.\r\n\r\nMutual funds, insurers participate\r\n\r\nOf the total anchor allocation, 3.88 crore shares were allotted to six domestic mutual funds, including WhiteOak Capital, Sundaram Mutual Fund, 360 ONE, PGIM India, JM Financial and Edelweiss, through 27 schemes.\r\n\r\nSBI Life Insurance and Edelweiss Life Insurance were allocated another 1.24 crore shares worth Rs 75 crore.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nDebt repayment gets bulk of IPO proceeds\r\n\r\nHorizon Industrial Parks plans to use Rs 2,250 crore of the net proceeds from the IPO to repay debt. The remaining funds will be used for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nThe company had outstanding borrowings of Rs 6,884.3 crore as of March 2026.\r\n\r\nDespite a sharp increase in revenue, the company's loss widened in FY26. Net loss rose to Rs 203.6 crore from Rs 178.7 crore in FY25, while revenue increased 77.1 percent to Rs 691.4 crore from Rs 390.3 crore.\r\n\r\nPan-India logistics network\r\n\r\nHorizon Industrial Parks is India's largest industrial and logistics infrastructure developer and operator, offering Grade A warehouses, industrial facilities and in-city centres across major industrial and consumption hubs.\r\n\r\nIts services also include cold storage, energy solutions, on-site staff accommodation, racking and material-handling equipment.\r\n\r\nThe company operates 45 assets across 10 cities, including Delhi-NCR, Mumbai, Bengaluru, Chennai, Pune, Hyderabad, Ahmedabad and Nagpur.\r\n\r\nJM Financial, Axis Capital, IIFL Capital Services, SBI Capital Markets and 360 ONE WAM are the merchant bankers managing the IPO.",
