            "id": "14006049",
            "headline": "Lalithaa Jewellery Mart raises Rs 508 crore from anchor investors ahead of Rs 1,700-crore IPO",
            "heading": "Lalithaa Jewellery Mart raises Rs 508 crore from anchor investors ahead of Rs 1,700-crore IPO",
            "intro": "Lalithaa Jewellery Mart IPO | The company aims to mobilise Rs 1,200 crore by issuing fresh shares, along side the selling of Rs 500 crore worth shares by promoter Kiran Kumar Jain via offer-for-sale.",
            "body": "Lalithaa Jewellery Mart, the jewellery retailer operating under the brand Lalithaa in sourthern India, has raised Rs 508.2 crore from 22 anchor investors, including Goldman Sachs, Morgan Stanley and ICICI Prudential AMC, ahead of its Rs 1,700-crore initial public offering (IPO).\r\n\r\nThe Chennai-based company allocated 2.52 crore equity shares to anchor investors at the upper end of the IPO price band of Rs 190-201 per share on August 14.\r\n\r\nThe public issue will open for subscription from August 17 to August 19.\r\n\r\nThe IPO comprises a fresh issue of shares worth Rs 1,200 crore and an offer for sale (OFS) of up to Rs 500 crore by promoter Kiran Kumar Jain.\r\n\r\nOf the total anchor allocation, 1.14 crore shares were allotted to four domestic mutual funds \u2014 ICICI Prudential AMC, Bandhan Mutual Fund, Samco Mutual Fund and Bank of India Mutual Fund \u2014 through nine schemes, according to the company's exchange filing.\r\n\r\nKotak Mahindra Life Insurance and Bajaj Life Insurance also invested Rs 43.19 crore for 21.49 lakh shares.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nExpansion plans\r\n\r\nLalithaa Jewellery Mart plans to use Rs 1,033.2 crore of the net proceeds from the fresh issue to set up 10 new stores across India. The remaining funds will be used for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nThe company currently operates 61 stores across 51 cities in southern India, selling gold, silver and diamond jewellery, with products tailored to regional preferences.\r\n\r\nThe retailer plans to use the IPO to expand its footprint.\r\n\r\nProfit jumps 177%\r\n\r\nLalithaa Jewellery Mart reported a sharp improvement in financial performance in FY26.\r\n\r\nIts profit rose 177 percent year-on-year to Rs 1,009.8 crore in the fiscal year ended March 2026, compared with Rs 364.7 crore in FY25.\r\n\r\nRevenue increased 48.1 percent to Rs 25,023.9 crore from Rs 16,897.3 crore during the same period.\r\n\r\nAnand Rathi Advisors and Equirus Capital are the merchant bankers managing the Lalithaa Jewellery Mart IPO.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/lalithaa-jewellery-mart-raises-rs-508-crore-from-anchor-investors-ahead-of-rs-1-700-crore-ipo-14006049.html",
