          "2": {
            "id": "14005957",
            "headline": "Avtar Steel files IPO papers to raise fresh capital of Rs 585 crore",
            "heading": "Avtar Steel files IPO papers to raise fresh capital of Rs 585 crore",
            "intro": "Avtar Steel IPO | The public issue comprises a fresh issue of shares worth Rs 585 crore, while promoter Sumit Jindal has proposed to sell up to 50 lakh shares through an offer for sale.",
            "body": "Delhi-based stainless-steel long and wire products maker Avtar Steel has filed its Draft Red Herring Prospectus (DRHP) with the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) to raise funds through an initial public offering (IPO).\r\n\r\nThe IPO comprises a fresh issue of shares worth Rs 585 crore, while promoter Sumit Jindal has proposed to sell up to 50 lakh shares through an offer for sale (OFS).\r\n\r\nThe company may also raise up to Rs 117 crore through a pre-IPO placement. Any amount raised through the pre-IPO round will be deducted from the fresh issue component.\r\n\r\nWhere Avtar Steel will use IPO proceeds\r\nAvtar Steel plans to use Rs 200 crore from the fresh issue to part-finance capital expenditure for a new specialty steel melting facility. The facility will manufacture special steel, stainless-steel blocks and blooms, while part of the funds will also be used to expand stainless-steel wire production at its existing facility.\r\n\r\nAnother Rs 200 crore will be used to repay debt. The company's total outstanding borrowings stood at Rs 339.3 crore as of July 2026. The remaining proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nThe company operates three manufacturing facilities in Sonipat, Haryana, with a combined capacity of 72,000 MTPA in steel melting, 1.2 lakh MTPA in wire rods and bars, and 24,000 MTPA in hot-rolling and cold-finishing.\r\n\r\nAvtar Steel financials\r\nAvtar Steel supplied stainless-steel long and wire products to 422 customers in FY26, including 265 repeat customers who contributed nearly 86 percent of its revenue.\r\n\r\nIts customers include Bansal Wire Industries, Goodluck India, Stellaris Specialities India, Vividh Wires, Ivy Creations UK, Goodluck Defense and Aerospace and Victura Technologies.\r\n\r\nThe company reported a 59.4 percent increase in profit to Rs 59.04 crore in FY26 from Rs 37 crore a year earlier. Revenue rose 13.5 percent to Rs 1,263.3 crore from Rs 1,112.8 crore.\r\n\r\nAvtar Steel competes with listed companies such as Mangalam Worldwide, Welspun Specialty Solutions and Mukand.\r\n\r\nAccording to a CARE report, India's stainless-steel market is projected to grow at a CAGR of 8.2 percent between FY26 and FY30, reaching around Rs 1.7 lakh crore by FY30. Infrastructure spending and growing applications in green hydrogen, smart urban infrastructure, renewable energy and tunnel construction are expected to support demand.\r\n\r\nThe company's shares are proposed to be listed on the BSE and NSE. Systematix Corporate Services and Elara Capital (India) are the merchant bankers for the IPO.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/avtar-steel-files-ipo-papers-to-raise-fresh-capital-of-rs-585-crore-14005957.html",
